Subject: Cantor Iterative Attention Procedure Loop P1 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 79f73f75-8d7f-452d-9013-0054245272bc
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Iterative_Attention_Procedure_Loop_P1.sop

& [Need]
  + P0 proves one model tool model call but deliberately rejects a legitimate READY successor
  + user intends chunked attention procedures and repeated inference checkpoints

& [Decision]
  + specify an explicit bounded host state machine whose model-visible continuity is a verified projection transcript and whose exact custody remains Cantor-owned

& [WhyNotAutoRun]
  + silently advancing all slices inside one call removes the intended opportunity for the model to observe progress and adjust at a checkpoint
  + unbounded model iteration risks cost drift loops and unverifiable partial completion

& [WhyNotImplementNow]
  + report cardinality replay stop and reentry semantics are materially larger than the proven P0 and require their own activation review

